[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868250140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868250140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868250140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q9gYc","user":{"login":"Chapien","id":2068976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2068976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien","html_url":"https://github.com/Chapien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T02:43:42Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T02:43:42Z","body":"Zoomed in screenshots of the cursor in case it is hard to find:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1426870d-5d41-4719-afa6-d726f38a8ddd)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ab405eff-a8e0-4260-b6a8-33cec419e535)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868250140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868906211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868906211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868906211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAAjj","user":{"login":"Chapien","id":2068976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2068976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien","html_url":"https://github.com/Chapien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T14:22:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T14:22:40Z","body":"For others finding this, there is a less system-level fix. `/usr/share/icons/default/index.theme` can be overridden by one of the following locations (both will work). This is ordered by priority; the top file gets considered first, followed by the remainder. \n`$HOME/.icons/default/index.theme`\n`$HOME/.local/share/icons/default/index.theme`\n`/usr/share/icons/default/index.theme`\n\nNote that `$HOME/.icons/default/index.theme` is technically only there for backwards compatibility (gnome still likes to use it sometimes, too), and that `$HOME/.local/share/icons/default/index.theme` should generally be favored.\n\nI do not however consider this issue fixed despite this workaround. Many modern, Wayland-based DEs do not create an index.theme -- the problem, as far as I can tell, is that `XCURSOR_THEME` is not required to be set on Wayland (indeed, it's technically only there at all for legacy reasons). Godot queries `XCURSOR_THEME` to determine your cursor. According to the XDG spec, if `XCURSOR_THEME` is not set, it falls back to the above locations (this is done automatically by the operating system -- even if KDE doesn't use XCURSOR_THEME, it will correctly point to the fallback locations when asked). The trouble is, this is all for _legacy_ purposes.\n\nHere's the code in quesiton:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/19bb18716ef08b811fec330cba4d35fbdb027bcc/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp#L4313 \n\nAnd here's the result of my `printenv` (just the XDG related stuff), demonstrating that `XCURSOR_THEME` is not set (and yet, despite that, my cursor works fine in pretty much every program, because there are alternative ways to query a user's cursor theme). My cursor is correct in Qt programs, SDL programs, GTK programs, and even the Godot 3 editor. The way bubblewrap handles system themes also means that in the flatpak, it uses the correct cursor as discussed before.\n\n```\nXAUTHORITY=/run/user/1000/xauth_GJJkUJ\nXDG_CONFIG_DIRS=/home/claire/.config/kdedefaults:/etc/xdg:/usr/share/kde-settings/kde-profile/default/xdg\nXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=KDE\nXDG_DATA_DIRS=<redacted>\nXDG_MENU_PREFIX=plasma-\nXDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000\nXDG_SEAT=seat0\nXDG_SEAT_PATH=/org/freedesktop/DisplayManager/Seat0\nXDG_SESSION_CLASS=user\nXDG_SESSION_DESKTOP=KDE\nXDG_SESSION_ID=2\nXDG_SESSION_PATH=/org/freedesktop/DisplayManager/Session1\nXDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland\nXDG_VTNR=2\nXKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT=us\nXKB_DEFAULT_MODEL=pc105\nXMODIFIERS=@im=none\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868906211/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868936602","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868936602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868936602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAH-a","user":{"login":"Chapien","id":2068976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2068976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien","html_url":"https://github.com/Chapien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T14:36:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T14:36:40Z","body":"A brief update: The current cursor theme on KDE is stored in: \n`$HOME/.config/kdedefaults/kcminputrc`\nDon't let the defaults in the name fool you, this should update whenever you change your cursor theme on KDE. Here's the contents of mine, as you can see it is identical to the files that XCURSOR pulls from (theme.index).\n```\n[Mouse]\ncursorTheme=breeze_cursors\n```\n\nI do not know how GNOME stores it. I _think_ it is stored inside `$HOME/.icons/default/index.theme`, leading to Godot being able to find it. But make no mistake, this is a happy accident. XCURSOR_THEME still is not being set, and XDG is just returning the first fallback location it can find to Godot.\n\nA potential fix would be to query `XDG_CONFIG_DIRS` instead of `XCURSOR_THEME`. From there, one could check for a `kcminputrc` file, falling down each fallback folder. If XDG_CONFIG_DIRS does not have the appropriate config file, it can then fall back to `XCURSOR_THEME`. That said, there's almost certainly a way to do this without reading a file, but I don't know enough about XDG or KDE to really give an answer as to what API to use.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868936602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868951128","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868951128","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868951128,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rALhY","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T15:01:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T15:01:01Z","body":"Since this is from the wayland server it seems like we should be using [cursor-shape-v1](https://wayland.app/protocols/cursor-shape-v1) to not have to deal with the current theme. GNOME were quite averse to doing this but they've since repented and implemented it. Not sure how other apps obtain the theme and we should likely still look into it as a fallback for when it's not implemented though","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868951128/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868958450","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868958450","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868958450,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rANTy","user":{"login":"Chapien","id":2068976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2068976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien","html_url":"https://github.com/Chapien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T15:13:41Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T15:13:41Z","body":"> Since this is from the wayland server it seems like we should be using [cursor-shape-v1](https://wayland.app/protocols/cursor-shape-v1) to not have to deal with the current theme. GNOME were quite averse to doing this but they've since repented and implemented it. Not sure how other apps obtain the theme and we should likely still look into it as a fallback for when it's not implemented though\n\nFrom my understadning, there's no reason you can't continue to use `XCURSOR_THEME` as the ultimate fallback. If nothing else works, `XCURSOR_THEME` will work on all setups that aren't either ancient or broken.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868958450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868960775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868960775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868960775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAN4H","user":{"login":"Chapien","id":2068976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg5NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2068976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien","html_url":"https://github.com/Chapien","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chapien/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T15:18:42Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T15:18:42Z","body":"As for falling back to the _correct_ theme... It should work on gnome, but I have no idea how to programmatically query kcminputrc that doesn't involve just reading the file.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868960775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868975765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868975765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868975765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rARiV","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T15:40:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T15:40:25Z","body":"Can confirm the bug. Also on KDE bit compiled without libdecor and you can clearly see the cursor changing between the decorations and main window.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868975765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868998212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106229#issuecomment-2868998212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106229","id":2868998212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAXBE","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T16:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T16:12:37Z","body":"I recall seeing this issue on Godot with X11 years ago (back in Godot 2.x if not earlier), but it hasn't been an issue for me with Godot for years. I'm using KDE for the record, but back then, I recall it happening both with KDE and Xfce.","author_ass